<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Saugor and Nerbudda Territories</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sagar-madhya-pradesh">Saugor</a> and Nerbudda Territories were a British-ruled region of central <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>, formed from lands taken from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Marathas</a> in 1818 around Sagar and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/narmada-river">Narmada</a> valley. Administered at times from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kolkata">Calcutta</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/agra">Agra</a>, they were enlarged by lands confiscated after the rising of 1857. In 1861 they were merged into the new <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/central-provinces">Central Provinces</a>.</p></div>
